 "content": "# Continual-ARC task-bd080f31\n\nObserved transformation from demo and confirmed test: for a 3x3 input, expand to 5x5 by duplicating the first and last rows and duplicating the first and last columns. Keep the middle row and column single. In other words output columns are [input col 1, input col 1, input col 2, input col 3, input col 3], and output rows are [input row 1, input row 1, input row 2, input row 3, input row 3], with corresponding values at intersections. Demo: [[6,5,5],[5,1,7],[4,5,2]] -> [[6,6,5,5,5],[6,6,5,5,5],[5,5,1,7,7],[4,4,5,2,2],[4,4,5,2,2]]. Confirmed test output: [[1,1,2,5,5],[1,1,2,5,5],[7,7,3,6,6],[7,7,6,5,5],[7,7,6,5,5]]."
